  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ViCo &#x2013; Vietnam&apos;s first national center for sustainability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Except Integrated Sustainability B.V. (Except) is a consultancy and design agency for sustainable development. The company has set up two sustainable innovation communities in Utrecht (UCo) and Rotterdam (Ro-Co) that bring together companies that are driven by sustainability, innovation and cooperative entrepreneurship. For this purpose, existing buildings have been renovated with a lot of attention being paid to reducing energy consumption and circular materials.Except now wants to implement this same concept in Vietnam. An Asian financial organisation is interested in investing in the first national innovation center for sustainability called Vietnam Community for sustainable entrepreneurship (ViCo) in Ho Chi Min City (HCMC). The building, approximately 3,000 m2, will provide workspace for the public and private sectors and local and international, especially Dutch social and environmentally driven companies. The focus will be on connecting stakeholders, providing a platform to easily exchange knowledge and establishing new cross-sector and multi-disciplinary partnerships to drive innovation and collaborative ideas for sustainability in Vietnam and the region.The aim is to purchase an outdated building and renovate it sustainably. This project will boost HCMC&apos;s efforts to build its reputation as a regional leader in sustainability.The study aims to determine which conditions are required to successfully develop ViCo, to investigate the suitability of the location(s) and to demonstrate a realistic sustainable and solid business model.</narrative>
  </description>
